    {
      "id": "starshield",
      "paragraph": "Starshield is a SpaceX service that uses satellites to carry military communications. A terminal is the equipment on the ground that connects to the service, and limits on its operation can affect when a connection is available. For example, a team trying to stop a drone may need to share its position while it is still in flight. On November 15, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said continued restrictions on the operating speed of Starshield terminals along the front and in occupied territory were hurting efforts to intercept Russian drones targeting power substations. AP and BBC reported his assessment. The reports leave open how much the restrictions contributed to missed interceptions.",
